    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 1 part 6 P2 run.log (specs/0013-formulas.md, "P2" and "Harness
    # runs"): the corpus run on both targets with --tool-arg --formula-sample,
    # the run log's two checks over every output (the comparison and the
    # computation), each with its controls, and the record pair.
    #
    # P2's acceptance, from "Harness runs", lo and lo_in ok in every case:
    #  - every entry outside the first worksheet, workbook.xml, the content
    #    types, the workbook relationships and the chain identical; the first
    #    worksheet and workbook.xml changed with the comparison's checks
    #    holding; the content types and the workbook relationships changed on
    #    the workbooks with a chain and identical on the others; the chain entry
    #    dropped (the diff's word for removed) on those;
    #  - totals, as corrected by specs/0013 "Planning rulings during P2
    #    (2026-09-23)", ruling 1, each derived from this log's own independent
    #    read of the inputs and never typed, each with a control: added 2 on
    #    each workbook with an A; replaced equal to the workbooks with an A and
    #    an F; chain_before equal to the chained workbooks; chain_after equal to
    #    chain_before minus the chained workbooks with an A; full_calc_before 0
    #    (no input carries the flag); full_calc_after equal to the workbooks
    #    with an A. Entry classes, the same ruling: the content types, the
    #    workbook relationships and the chain entry change or go only on the
    #    chained workbooks with an A; workbook.xml and the first worksheet
    #    change only on the workbooks with an A; the workbooks without an A are
    #    byte-identical, files_identical yes on exactly those;
    #  - the comparison and the computation holding on every output.
    #
    # WRITTEN FOR M1 part 6 P2 from P1's run script (records/logs/m1p6-p1/
    # run.log), carrying its rules: lines 1 to 3 are the command, the invocation
    # and about:, then the three shape greps over this file, then the phase's
    # commits by role read from git; no commit id is typed here. What differs,
    # and why:
    #  1. The operation is --formula-sample, and the log's own checks are
    #     p2check.py (printed below with its sha256): zipfile and expat, sharing
    #     no code with the library or the tool, making its own pick of A, F and
    #     M. Its modes: pick (counts only), parts (four part names to a file the
    #     log reads and never prints), cmp (the comparison, fifteen flags) and
    #     computed (the computation through the pinned LibreOffice image).
    #  2. The control pairs are the three fictional workbooks fixtures.py builds
    #     (printed below): A and F with a chain, A without F, neither with a
    #     chain. The phase commit's host tool edits each; its line must be the
    #     hand count, both checks must hold, and every plant must turn its own
    #     flag and no other. Every flag must be turned by some applied plant,
    #     flag by flag (specs/0012 P2 ruling 3). The comparison's fifteen plants
    #     and one computation plant are then run on one real output as well.
    #  3. The computation converts each output once more with --convert-to xlsx
    #     through the runner's own route and image (scripts/passthrough-run.sh's
    #     lo_check: podman run --rm --network=none --userns=keep-id, the input's
    #     directory read-only as /in), into <scratch>, and deletes the converted
    #     file after the read. From specs/0013's Facts, this image recomputes
    #     every formula on load whether or not fullCalcOnLoad is set, so this
    #     check proves that the written text computes and does not measure the
    #     flag.
    #  4. P1 verification ruling 9: before the run, the four run directories of
    #     P1's superseded attempts under <corpus>/runs are removed. Their names
    #     are not typed: each is read from git as P1's code commits by role and
    #     the date of P1's committed record pair, and the name of P1's final run
    #     directory, which stays, likewise. Each name is checked to be of the
    #     date-and-commit form and a real directory directly under runs/ before
    #     it is removed, and nothing else is removed.
    #  5. P1 verification ruling 6: the build directory is named once,
    #     <scratch>/p2/target, the same in header and body. It is SHARED with
    #     this phase's gate log, which built into it first: this log's build,
    #     from the phase commit's tree extracted by git archive, replaces the
    #     binaries there, and this log prints the sha256 of the four it runs.
    #     Those may differ from the ones gate.log hashed, since the source path
    #     differs.
    #  6. ORDER: the control pairs run on the real host binary first, and the
    #     log stops before touching the corpus if any of their checks failed.
    #     Only then are P1's superseded run directories removed (item 4) and the
    #     corpus run started, as the coordinator's handoff orders it.
    #  7. The status check counts this phase's logs and record pair
    #     (records/logs/m1p6-p2/ and records/m1p6-p2-*) as the phase's files,
    #     and specs/0013-formulas.md modified as planning's.
    #
    # None of the three shapes specs/0001 forbids appears here: every compound
    # condition is a named function and every negated one goes through isnot,
    # whose control is below; the shapes are described rather than written out.
    #
    # THE CELLS THAT DIFFER: four references, A, F and the two new cells (three
    # without F), since the tool sets A to Number(21) for the computation
    # (specs/0013 "Planning rulings during P2", ruling 2, amending "Harness
    # runs"). The comparison follows the tool.
    #
    # ATTEMPT 4. Attempt 3 (same commit, -c, never created) stopped before
    # the corpus run: its script defined its own count_lines, which shadowed
    # the one scripts/counting.sh defines and failed the counting controls.
    # The fix was deleting that definition. This attempt takes RUN_TAG -c.
    #
    # ATTEMPT 3. Attempt 2 (same commit, -b) had every check as expected and is
    # superseded by independent check 1's F1 (the ruling-9 block printed the
    # four P1 directories only as absent; their removal, made by attempt 1, is
    # now quoted verbatim from attempt 1's kept log, and P2's own superseded run
    # directories are printed as kept, pending planning), F6 (a typed 27 in
    # derived checks; every workbook count is now compared with the manifest
    # rows the log reads, with a control) and F8 (files_identical is now also
    # checked as the set of ids without A, with a swapped-id control). This
    # attempt takes RUN_TAG -c.
    #
    # ATTEMPT 2. Attempt 1 at the same phase commit ran to the end with three
    # UNEXPECTED verdicts, all one fact: chain_after totalled 6 against the
    # spec's uncorrected 0, because 6 of the 9 chained workbooks have no A.
    # Planning's ruling 1 corrected the expectation, not the tool. Its
    # SERIALIZED line was also false: the implementing session's scan dry run
    # overlapped it (ruling 3(e)). This attempt asserts ruling 1's derived
    # expectations, runs alone, and takes RUN_TAG -b for a fresh run directory;
    # the record stem is unchanged. Attempt 1's log, stderr, record pair and
    # script are hashed in the rerun header under role names. The status check
    # counts specs/0013-formulas.md, modified and uncommitted, as planning's
    # file (it goes in P3's first doc commit), printed with its sha256.
    #
    # Workbooks appear as ids only, and the checks print counts and yes/no
    # flags only: no reference, no cell value, no formula text (a composed text
    # would reveal A's reference), no sheet name and no part name. The corpus
    # directory is written <corpus>.
    #
    # Usage: m1p6-p2-run.sh <phase commit> > <scratch file>; the caller moves the
    # output to records/logs/m1p6-p2/run.log. Started detached and polled.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)/$(basename "$0")
    P2DIR=$(dirname "$SELF")
    SCR=$(dirname "$P2DIR")
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    . scripts/counting.sh
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never
    CORPUS=${EMEND_CORPUS_DIR:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    LO_IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    REC_DIR=$P2DIR/out
    BT=$P2DIR/target
    HEAD_SHA=$(git rev-parse HEAD)
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    EDIT=--formula-sample
    fail=0
    
    nbad=0; nunexp=0
    note() {
      echo "  $1: $2"
      if [ "$2" != as-expected ]; then
        fail=1; nbad=$((nbad + 1))
        [ "$2" = UNEXPECTED ] && nunexp=$((nunexp + 1))
      fi
    }
    is() { if "$@"; then echo as-expected; else echo UNEXPECTED; fi; }
    isnot() { if "$@"; then echo UNEXPECTED; else echo as-expected; fi; }
    hide() { sed "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g; s#$SCR#<scratch>#g; s#$MAIN#<repo>#g; s#$HOME#<home>#g"; }
    bad() { fail=1; nbad=$((nbad + 1)); }
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    mkdir -p "$REC_DIR" || exit 2
    W=$(mktemp -d "$P2DIR/w.XXXXXX") || exit 2
    trap 'rm -rf "$W"' EXIT INT TERM HUP
    
    nrows() { awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    columns_resolve() {
      awk -F'\t' -v want="$2" '
        NR == 1 {
          seen = 1
          for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) have[$i] = 1
          n = split(want, w, " ")
          for (j = 1; j <= n; j++) if (!(w[j] in have)) miss++
          exit
        }
        END { exit (seen != 1 || miss > 0) }' "$1"
    }
    count_where() {
      awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" -v v="$3" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next }
        k && $k == v { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    sum_col() {
      awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next }
        k { n += $k } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    # kv <line> <key>: the value of key=value in a line split on tabs or spaces.
    kv() { printf '%s\n' "$1" | tr '\t ' '\n\n' | sed -n "s/^$2=//p" | head -1; }
    kvn() {
      local v
      v=$(kv "$1" "$2")
      case "$v" in '' | *[!0-9]*) echo 0 ;; *) echo "$v" ;; esac
    }
    
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    is_head() { full_sha "$1" && [ "$1" = "$HEAD_SHA" ]; }
    if ! is_head "$C"; then echo "the phase commit must be HEAD as a full sha, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    inv_path=$SELF
    case "$inv_path" in
      "$MAIN"/*) inv_path="<repo>/${inv_path#"$MAIN"/}" ;;
      "$SCR"/*) inv_path="<scratch>/${inv_path#"$SCR"/}" ;;
      /*) inv_path="<scratch>/$(basename "$inv_path")" ;;
    esac
    echo "invocation: bash $inv_path $*"
    echo "about: M1 part 6 P2 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $HEAD_SHA"
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $HEAD_SHA"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(is full_sha "$C")"
    note "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(is is_head "$C")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(isnot is_head "$NULL_SHA")"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" \
      "$(isnot is_head "$(printf '%s' "$C" | cut -c1-7)")"
    note "control: isnot reports a passing command as UNEXPECTED, so it can fail" \
      "$(is [ "$(isnot true)" = UNEXPECTED ])"
    
    # The three shape greps over this script's own file. The patterns are
    # bracket forms, which do not match themselves; the fixtures are assembled
    # by printf.
    SHAPE_CHAIN='[$][(](yn|is|isnot) .*(&&|[|][|])'
    SHAPE_BANG='[$][(](yn|is|isnot) [!]'
    SHAPE_ASSIGN='[$][(](yn|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z_0-9]*='
    printf 'x %s(is [ a = a ] && [ b = b ])\n' '$' >"$W/shape-chain"
    printf 'x %s(is %s f a b)\n' '$' '!' >"$W/shape-bang"
    printf 'x %s(isnot %s%s /usr/bin/grep -q x f)\n' '$' 'LC_ALL' '=C' >"$W/shape-assign"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps over this script's own file"
    echo "command: sha256sum <scratch>/p2/$(basename "$SELF")"
    echo "  $(sha256sum <"$SELF" | cut -d' ' -f1)  $(wc -c <"$SELF") bytes"
    shape_hit=0
    for shape in chain bang assign; do
      case $shape in chain) pat=$SHAPE_CHAIN ;; bang) pat=$SHAPE_BANG ;; assign) pat=$SHAPE_ASSIGN ;; esac
      echo "command: count_matches -E <the $shape pattern> over <scratch>/p2/$(basename "$SELF"), and over a control fixture holding the $shape shape"
      echo "  the $shape pattern: $pat"
      on_self=$(count_matches -E "$pat" "$SELF")
      on_ctl=$(count_matches -E "$pat" "$W/shape-$shape")
      echo "  hits on this script: $on_self; hits on the control: $on_ctl"
      note "the $shape shape: no hit on this script" "$(is [ "$on_self" = 0 ])"
      note "control: the $shape pattern finds its shape in the fixture, through the same form" "$(is [ "$on_ctl" = 1 ])"
      [ "$on_self" = 0 ] || shape_hit=1
    done
    if [ "$shape_hit" != 0 ]; then
      echo "a shape grep hit this script (or could not read it): stopping before any case"
      exit 1
    fi
    
    # code_commits <part>: the code commits of one phase by role, oldest first,
    # as "<sha> <subject>" lines; the planning doc commits are set apart.
    code_commits() {
      git log --reverse --format='%H %s' --grep="^M1 part 6 $1: " | LC_ALL=C "$G" -v -F 'commit planning docs'
    }
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits, by role, read from git"
    echo "command: git log --reverse --format='%H %s' --grep='^M1 part 6 P2: ' (planning doc commits printed and set apart)"
    git log --reverse --format='%H %s' --grep='^M1 part 6 P2: ' >"$W/phase-commits"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -F 'commit planning docs' "$W/phase-commits" | sed 's/^/    planning doc commit: /'
    code_commits P2 >"$W/code-commits"
    awk '{ printf "    code commit %d: %s\n", NR, $0 }' "$W/code-commits"
    ncode=$(count_lines "$W/code-commits")
    last_code=$(tail -n 1 "$W/code-commits" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    first_code=$(head -n 1 "$W/code-commits" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "  code commits: $ncode; the last: $last_code"
    last_is_phase() { [ -n "$last_code" ] && [ "$last_code" = "$C" ]; }
    first_is_phase() { [ -n "$first_code" ] && [ "$first_code" = "$C" ]; }
    note "the last code commit, read from git, is the phase commit given to this script" "$(is last_is_phase)"
    note "control: the first code commit is not the phase commit" "$(isnot first_is_phase)"
    note "P2 has three code commits" "$(is [ "$ncode" = 3 ])"
    echo "command: git rev-parse --short <the phase commit>"
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short "$C")
    echo "  $SHORT"
    RUN_TAG=${RUN_TAG:-}
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT$RUN_TAG
    OUT=$CORPUS/runs/$RUN
    STEM=m1p6-p2-$DATE-$SHORT
    echo "  run directory: <corpus>/runs/$RUN; record stem: $STEM; build directory: <scratch>/p2/target"
    
    echo "phase: Milestone 1 part 6 P2 (specs/0013-formulas.md) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" \
            "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then
        echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"
      fi
    fi
    echo "SERIALIZED: produced with no other run in flight."
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go"
    echo "  to a scratch file, polled from later calls."
    echo "TERMS: this log's two builds finish before the runner starts; order host"
    echo "  then i686; no mid-run tuning, and a copy or conversion that timed out"
    echo "  or was killed would be recorded and listed apart, never rerun with a"
    echo "  larger value."
    echo "TIMEOUT CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN: --timeout 300 for the copy child, the"
    echo "  figure part 4's, part 5's and P1's corpus runs used; --lo-timeout 600"
    echo "  per conversion, the runner's and the computation's alike. Neither is"
    echo "  tuned during the run; each workbook's wall time is in the record's"
    echo "  summary table (wall_s)."
    echo "THE COMPUTATION DOES NOT MEASURE THE FLAG: the pinned image"
    echo "  $LO_IMAGE recomputes every formula on load whether or"
    echo "  not fullCalcOnLoad is set (specs/0013, Facts planning checked), so the"
    echo "  computation proves that each written text computes, and says nothing"
    echo "  about whether Excel would honour the flag or a cached value."
    echo "Workbooks are cited by id only. The corpus directory's PATH is written"
    echo "  <corpus> wherever this log prints a path; its NAME appears in the"
    echo "  script printed below, in the line that takes the default CLAUDE.md"
    echo "  gives. What is private is the corpus's contents and file names."
    
    echo
    echo "## script"
    echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' <this script>; sha256 $(sha256sum <"$SELF" | cut -d' ' -f1), $(wc -c <"$SELF") bytes"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' scripts/counting.sh; sha256 $(sha256sum <scripts/counting.sh | cut -d' ' -f1)"
    sed 's/^/    /' scripts/counting.sh
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then
      echo "  the counting controls did not all hold"
      bad
    fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the checks this log runs (python3, zipfile and expat), copied once"
    for f in p2check.py fixtures.py; do
      cp "$P2DIR/$f" "$W/$f" || exit 2
      echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' <scratch>/p2/$f; sha256 $(sha256sum <"$W/$f" | cut -d' ' -f1), $(wc -c <"$W/$f") bytes"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$W/$f"
    done
    PC=$W/p2check.py
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase commit's tree and this log's own builds"
    PHASE_FILES='^(\?\?| ?[MARCD]) (records/logs/m1p6-p2/|records/m1p6-p2-)'
    PLANNING_FILES='^ M specs/0013-formulas[.]md$'
    # status_accounted <all> <phase> [<planning>]: every status line is this
    # phase's logs or record pair, or planning's file modified.
    status_accounted() {
      [ "$1" != error ] && [ "$2" != error ] && [ "${3:-0}" != error ] && [ "$1" = "$(($2 + ${3:-0}))" ]
    }
    planning_status() {
      st_plan=$(run_matches -E "$PLANNING_FILES" git status --porcelain)
      git status --porcelain | LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$PLANNING_FILES" | cut -c4- |
        while IFS= read -r pf; do echo "  planning's file $pf: sha256 $(sha256sum <"$pf" | cut -d' ' -f1)"; done
    }
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    st_before=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_before_phase=$(run_matches -E "$PHASE_FILES" git status --porcelain)
    planning_status
    echo "  status lines before the build: $st_before; of them this phase's logs or record pair: $st_before_phase; planning's files modified: $st_plan"
    note "every change in the working tree before the build is this phase's logs or record pair, or planning's file" \
      "$(is status_accounted "$st_before" "$st_before_phase" "$st_plan")"
    printf '?? records/logs/m1p6-p2/\n?? crates/emend/src/x.rs\n' >"$W/status-ctl"
    st_ctl_all=$(count_lines "$W/status-ctl")
    st_ctl_phase=$(count_matches -E "$PHASE_FILES" "$W/status-ctl")
    printf ' M specs/0013-formulas.md\n M specs/0001-bootstrap.md\n' >"$W/status-plan-ctl"
    st_ctl_plan=$(count_matches -E "$PLANNING_FILES" "$W/status-plan-ctl")
    note "control: the planning form counts specs/0013 and not another spec ($st_ctl_plan of 2)" \
      "$(is [ "$st_ctl_plan" = 1 ])"
    note "control: the same test refuses a status holding a source change" \
      "$(isnot status_accounted "$st_ctl_all" "$st_ctl_phase")"
    SRC=$W/src
    mkdir -p "$SRC" || exit 2
    echo "command: git archive <the phase commit> | tar -x -C <scratch>/p2/w/src"
    git archive "$C" | tar -x -C "$SRC"
    arc=$?
    note "git archive of the phase commit extracts" "$(is [ "$arc" -eq 0 ])"
    tree_files=$(git ls-tree -r --name-only "$C" | wc -l)
    src_files=$(cd "$SRC" && find . -type f | wc -l)
    echo "  files in the phase commit's tree: $tree_files; files extracted: $src_files"
    note "every file of the phase commit's tree was extracted" "$(is [ "$tree_files" = "$src_files" ])"
    same_as_tree() { cmp -s "$SRC/$1" "$MAIN/$1"; }
    for s in scripts/passthrough-run.sh scripts/passthrough-record.py scripts/counting.sh; do
      echo "  $s: sha256 $(sha256sum <"$SRC/$s" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
      note "$s as extracted is the working tree's file" "$(is same_as_tree "$s")"
    done
    printf 'x\n' >"$W/not-a-script"
    note "control: the same comparison refuses a file that differs" \
      "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/not-a-script" "$MAIN/scripts/counting.sh")"
    I686=i686-unknown-linux-musl
    build() {
      local label=$1
      shift
      echo "command: cargo build --locked -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff $* (in the extracted tree, CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<scratch>/p2/target)"
      (cd "$SRC" && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$BT cargo build --locked -p emend-copy -p xlsx-diff "$@") \
        >"$W/build-$label.out" 2>"$W/build-$label.err"
      local rc=$?
      echo "  exit $rc; the build's last line: $(tail -1 "$W/build-$label.err" | hide | sed 's/ in [0-9.]*s$//')"
      build_rc=$rc
    }
    build host
    note "the host debug build of the phase commit succeeds" "$(is [ "$build_rc" -eq 0 ])"
    build i686 --target "$I686"
    note "the i686 debug build of the phase commit succeeds" "$(is [ "$build_rc" -eq 0 ])"
    PT_host=$BT/debug/emend-copy
    XD_host=$BT/debug/xlsx-diff
    PT_i686=$BT/$I686/debug/emend-copy
    XD_i686=$BT/$I686/debug/xlsx-diff
    echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over the four binaries"
    for b in "$PT_host" "$XD_host" "$PT_i686" "$XD_i686"; do
      if [ -x "$b" ]; then
        echo "  <scratch>/${b#"$SCR"/}: sha256 $(sha256sum <"$b" | cut -d' ' -f1), bytes $(wc -c <"$b")"
      else
        echo "  <scratch>/${b#"$SCR"/}: MISSING"; bad
      fi
    done
    header_hex() { od -A n -t x1 -j "$2" -N "$3" "$1" | tr -d ' \n'; }
    is_i686_elf() {
      [ "$(header_hex "$1" 0 4)" = 7f454c46 ] || return 1
      [ "$(header_hex "$1" 4 1)" = 01 ] || return 1
      [ "$(header_hex "$1" 18 2)" = 0300 ]
    }
    note "the i686 emend-copy is a 32-bit ELF for i386" "$(is is_i686_elf "$PT_i686")"
    note "control: the same test refuses the host emend-copy" "$(isnot is_i686_elf "$PT_host")"
    
    # The expected tool line for one workbook, from p2check.py's pick line alone:
    # added 2 with A; replaced 1 with A and F; chain_after the chain when
    # nothing was recorded; full_calc_after 1 with A, else as read; cells_after
    # grows by the two added; read_back the added and the replaced.
    expected_line() {
      local p=$1 a f ch cells flag
      a=$(kvn "$p" a); f=$(kvn "$p" f); ch=$(kvn "$p" chain); cells=$(kvn "$p" cells); flag=$(kvn "$p" calc_pr_flag)
      local added=$((2 * a)) replaced=$((a * f))
      local chain_after=$((ch * (1 - a))) full_after=$flag
      [ "$a" = 1 ] && full_after=1
      printf 'formula\tadded=%d\treplaced=%d\tchain_before=%d\tchain_after=%d\tfull_calc_before=%d\tfull_calc_after=%d\tcells_before=%d\tcells_after=%d\tread_back=%d' \
        "$added" "$replaced" "$ch" "$chain_after" "$flag" "$full_after" "$cells" "$((cells + added))" "$((added + replaced))"
    }
    line_agrees() { [ "$1" = "$(expected_line "$2")" ]; }
    # cmp_holds <cmp line>: found, planted, and every flag yes.
    cmp_holds() {
      case "$1" in found=1\ planted=yes\ *) ;; *) return 1 ;; esac
      [ "$(printf '%s' "$1" | tr ' ' '\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -c '=no$')" = 0 ]
    }
    # computed_holds <computed line> <f>: converted, and the two new cells and F
    # (when there is one) computed as the spec expects.
    computed_holds() {
      local want_f=yes
      [ "$2" = 0 ] && want_f=na
      [ "$1" = "computed=1 planted=yes v_new1=yes v_new2=yes v_f=$want_f" ]
    }
    # computed_plant_caught <computed line> <plant> <f>: the planted value reads
    # no and the others read as on a sound output.
    computed_plant_caught() {
      local want_f=yes v1=yes v2=yes
      [ "$3" = 0 ] && want_f=na
      case $2 in v_new1) v1=no ;; v_new2) v2=no ;; v_f) want_f=no ;; esac
      [ "$1" = "computed=1 planted=yes v_new1=$v1 v_new2=$v2 v_f=$want_f" ]
    }
    # only_flag_no <line> <flag>: the named flag reads no and no other does.
    only_flag_no() {
      [ "$(kv "$1" "$2")" = no ] || return 1
      [ "$(printf '%s' "$1" | tr ' ' '\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -c '=no$')" = 1 ]
    }
    CMP_FLAGS='ws_prefix_same ws_suffix_same changed_as_edited a_as_edited f_as_edited added_as_edited texts_ok nothing_removed wb_outside_same calc_pr_as_edited chain_entry_ok chain_override_ok chain_rel_ok rels_rest_same types_rest_same'
    
    echo
    echo "## the control pairs: the phase commit's host tool on the fictional fixtures"
    FX=$W/fx
    mkdir -p "$FX"
    echo "command: python3 fixtures.py <scratch>/p2/w/fx"
    python3 "$W/fixtures.py" "$FX"
    # By hand, from fixtures.py: c-af-chain has A (B1), F (C1), M 4, a chain and
    # 7 cells; c-a-nof has A (A2), no F, M 2, no chain and 3 cells; c-neither has
    # no A, an F, a chain and 2 cells.
    declare -A HAND_PICK HAND_LINE
    HAND_PICK[c-af-chain]='found=1 a=1 f=1 chain=1 cells=7 calc_prs=1 calc_pr_flag=0'
    HAND_PICK[c-a-nof]='found=1 a=1 f=0 chain=0 cells=3 calc_prs=1 calc_pr_flag=0'
    HAND_PICK[c-neither]='found=1 a=0 f=1 chain=1 cells=2 calc_prs=1 calc_pr_flag=0'
    HAND_LINE[c-af-chain]=$(printf 'formula\tadded=2\treplaced=1\tchain_before=1\tchain_after=0\tfull_calc_before=0\tfull_calc_after=1\tcells_before=7\tcells_after=9\tread_back=3')
    HAND_LINE[c-a-nof]=$(printf 'formula\tadded=2\treplaced=0\tchain_before=0\tchain_after=0\tfull_calc_before=0\tfull_calc_after=1\tcells_before=3\tcells_after=5\tread_back=2')
    HAND_LINE[c-neither]=$(printf 'formula\tadded=0\treplaced=0\tchain_before=1\tchain_after=1\tfull_calc_before=0\tfull_calc_after=0\tcells_before=2\tcells_after=2\tread_back=0')
    declare -A TURNED
    for fx in c-af-chain c-a-nof c-neither; do
      in=$FX/$fx.xlsx
      out=$FX/$fx-out.xlsx
      p=$(python3 "$PC" pick "$in")
      echo "  $fx pick: $p"
      note "$fx: the pick is the hand count" "$(is [ "$p" = "${HAND_PICK[$fx]}" ])"
      echo "command: <scratch>/p2/target/debug/emend-copy <fixture> <out> --formula-sample"
      t=$("$PT_host" "$in" "$out" --formula-sample 2>"$W/fx-err")
      rc=$?
      echo "  $fx exit $rc; stderr bytes $(wc -c <"$W/fx-err"); the tool's line: $(printf '%s' "$t" | tr '\t' ' ')"
      note "$fx: the tool's line is the hand count" "$(is [ "$t" = "${HAND_LINE[$fx]}" ])"
      note "$fx: the line the log expects from its own pick is the same" "$(is line_agrees "$t" "$p")"
      c=$(python3 "$PC" cmp "$in" "$out")
      echo "  $fx cmp: $c"
      note "$fx: the comparison holds on the tool's output" "$(is cmp_holds "$c")"
      for flag in $CMP_FLAGS; do
        pl=$(python3 "$PC" cmp "$in" "$out" --plant "$flag")
        if [ "$(kv "$pl" planted)" = yes ]; then
          if only_flag_no "$pl" "$flag"; then
            TURNED[$flag]=$((${TURNED[$flag]:-0} + 1))
            echo "    $fx plant $flag: applied; $flag alone reads no"
          else
            echo "    $fx plant $flag: applied; $flag did NOT turn alone"
            bad
          fi
        else
          echo "    $fx plant $flag: does not apply to this pair"
        fi
      done
      if [ "$(kv "$p" a)" = 1 ]; then
        cm=$(python3 "$PC" computed "$in" "$out" "$W/lo-work" "$LO_IMAGE" 600)
        echo "  $fx computed: $cm"
        note "$fx: the computation holds on the tool's output" "$(is computed_holds "$cm" "$(kv "$p" f)")"
        for plant in v_new1 v_new2 v_f; do
          cp=$(python3 "$PC" computed "$in" "$out" "$W/lo-work" "$LO_IMAGE" 600 --plant "$plant")
          if [ "$(kv "$cp" planted)" = yes ]; then
            echo "    $fx computed plant $plant: $cp"
            if computed_plant_caught "$cp" "$plant" "$(kv "$p" f)"; then
              TURNED[$plant]=$((${TURNED[$plant]:-0} + 1))
              echo "    $fx: the planted $plant is caught, and nothing else moves"
            else
              echo "    $fx: the planted $plant is NOT caught alone"
              bad
            fi
          else
            echo "    $fx computed plant $plant: does not apply to this pair"
          fi
        done
      else
        cm=$(python3 "$PC" computed "$in" "$out" "$W/lo-work" "$LO_IMAGE" 600)
        note "$fx: with no A there is nothing to compute ($cm)" "$(is [ "$cm" = computed=na ])"
      fi
      converted_left() { [ -e "$W/lo-work" ]; }
      note "$fx: no converted file outlives the read" "$(isnot converted_left)"
    done
    for flag in $CMP_FLAGS v_new1 v_new2 v_f; do
      note "every check's flag $flag was turned by an applied plant (${TURNED[$flag]:-0})" \
        "$(is [ "${TURNED[$flag]:-0}" -ge 1 ])"
    done
    note "control: line_agrees refuses the hand line against another pick" \
      "$(isnot line_agrees "${HAND_LINE[c-af-chain]}" "${HAND_PICK[c-a-nof]}")"
    note "control: cmp_holds refuses a line with one flag no" \
      "$(isnot cmp_holds 'found=1 planted=yes a=1 texts_ok=no')"
    note "control: cmp_holds refuses a line whose plant did not apply" \
      "$(isnot cmp_holds 'found=1 planted=no a=1')"
    note "control: computed_plant_caught refuses a plant that moved a second value" \
      "$(isnot computed_plant_caught 'computed=1 planted=yes v_new1=no v_new2=no v_f=yes' v_new1 1)"
    note "control: computed_holds refuses v_f na on a workbook with F" \
      "$(isnot computed_holds 'computed=1 planted=yes v_new1=yes v_new2=yes v_f=na' 1)"
    
    if [ "$fail" -ne 0 ]; then
      echo "a check before the corpus run failed ($nbad so far): stopping before any run directory is touched"
      echo "verdict rows other than as-expected: $nbad; of them marked UNEXPECTED: $nunexp"
      echo "run log checks all as expected: no"
      exit 1
    fi
    echo
    echo "## P1's superseded run directories, removed (P1 verification ruling 9)"
    # The names are read from git: P1's three code commits by role, and the date
    # and the last code commit of P1's committed record pair. P1's attempts ran
    # at code commit 1 (twice, the second with the suffix -b), at code commit 2
    # and at code commit 3; its final run, at code commit 3 with -b, stays.
    echo "command: git log --reverse --format='%H %s' --grep='^M1 part 6 P1: ' (planning doc commits set apart)"
    code_commits P1 >"$W/p1-commits"
    awk '{ printf "    P1 code commit %d: %s\n", NR, $0 }' "$W/p1-commits"
    np1=$(count_lines "$W/p1-commits")
    note "P1 has three code commits" "$(is [ "$np1" = 3 ])"
    p1_short() { git rev-parse --short "$(sed -n "${1}p" "$W/p1-commits" | cut -d' ' -f1)"; }
    echo "command: git ls-files 'records/m1p6-p1-*.md'"
    p1_record=$(git ls-files 'records/m1p6-p1-*.md')
    echo "  $p1_record"
    p1_stem=$(basename "$p1_record" .md)
    p1_date=$(printf '%s' "$p1_stem" | sed -n 's/^m1p6-p1-\([0-9]\{4\}-[0-9]\{2\}-[0-9]\{2\}\)-[0-9a-f]*$/\1/p')
    p1_last=$(printf '%s' "$p1_stem" | sed -n 's/^m1p6-p1-[0-9-]\{10\}-\([0-9a-f]*\)$/\1/p')
    S1=$(p1_short 1); S2=$(p1_short 2); S3=$(p1_short 3)
    echo "  P1 record date: $p1_date; its commit: $p1_last; code commits' short ids: $S1 $S2 $S3"
    record_is_last() { [ -n "$p1_last" ] && [ "$p1_last" = "$S3" ]; }
    note "P1's record pair names its third code commit" "$(is record_is_last)"
    KEEP=$p1_date-$S3-b
    STALE="$p1_date-$S1 $p1_date-$S1-b $p1_date-$S2 $p1_date-$S3"
    RUNS=$CORPUS/runs
    # removable <runs dir> <name>: the name is of the date-and-commit form, and
    # <runs dir>/<name> is a directory, not a symbolic link, whose parent is the
    # runs directory itself.
    removable() {
      printf '%s' "$2" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9a-f]{7,12}(-[a-z])?$' || return 1
      [ -d "$1/$2" ] || return 1
      [ -L "$1/$2" ] && return 1
      [ "$(cd "$1/$2/.." && pwd -P)" = "$(cd "$1" && pwd -P)" ]
    }
    mkdir -p "$W/runs-ctl/2026-01-01-abcdef0" "$W/runs-ctl/not-a-run" "$W/elsewhere"
    : >"$W/runs-ctl/2026-01-01-abcdef1"
    ln -s "$W/elsewhere" "$W/runs-ctl/2026-01-01-abcdef2"
    note "control: removable accepts a directory of the form" "$(is removable "$W/runs-ctl" 2026-01-01-abcdef0)"
    note "control: removable refuses a file of the form" "$(isnot removable "$W/runs-ctl" 2026-01-01-abcdef1)"
    note "control: removable refuses a symbolic link of the form" "$(isnot removable "$W/runs-ctl" 2026-01-01-abcdef2)"
    note "control: removable refuses a directory of another form" "$(isnot removable "$W/runs-ctl" not-a-run)"
    note "control: removable refuses a path that climbs out" "$(isnot removable "$W/runs-ctl" ../elsewhere)"
    kept_is_stale() { case " $STALE " in *" $KEEP "*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    note "P1's final run directory is not among the four" "$(isnot kept_is_stale)"
    for name in $STALE; do
      if [ -e "$RUNS/$name" ] || [ -L "$RUNS/$name" ]; then
        if removable "$RUNS" "$name"; then
          echo "command: rm -rf -- <corpus>/runs/$name"
          rm -rf -- "${RUNS:?}/$name"
          gone() { [ ! -e "$RUNS/$name" ]; }
          note "<corpus>/runs/$name removed" "$(is gone)"
        else
          echo "  <corpus>/runs/$name: NOT a run directory of the form; left in place"
          bad
        fi
      else
        echo "  <corpus>/runs/$name: absent already; nothing to remove"
      fi
    done
    kept_there() { removable "$RUNS" "$KEEP"; }
    note "P1's final run directory <corpus>/runs/$KEEP is still there" "$(is kept_there)"
    # The removals themselves were made by this log's attempt 1 (independent
    # check 1's F1): its printed lines are quoted here verbatim from the kept,
    # role-named copy of that log, whose hash is printed by the command below.
    A1_LOG=$P2DIR/out/superseded/run-roles/run-attempt1.log
    echo "command: sha256sum <scratch>/p2/out/superseded/run-roles/run-attempt1.log"
    if [ -f "$A1_LOG" ]; then
      echo "  $(sha256sum <"$A1_LOG" | cut -d' ' -f1)  $(wc -c <"$A1_LOG") bytes"
    else
      echo "  MISSING"; bad
    fi
    echo "command: grep -E '^(command: rm -rf -- <corpus>/runs/|  <corpus>/runs/.* removed: )' <that log>, quoted verbatim"
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -E '^(command: rm -rf -- <corpus>/runs/|  <corpus>/runs/.* removed: )' "$A1_LOG" >"$W/a1-removals" 2>/dev/null
    sed 's/^/    | /' "$W/a1-removals"
    # removed_in_a1 <name>: attempt 1 printed both the command and an
    # as-expected removal for the name.
    removed_in_a1() {
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxF "command: rm -rf -- <corpus>/runs/$1" "$W/a1-removals" || return 1
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -qxF "  <corpus>/runs/$1 removed: as-expected" "$W/a1-removals"
    }
    for name in $STALE; do
      note "attempt 1 printed the removal of <corpus>/runs/$name" "$(is removed_in_a1 "$name")"
      absent_now() { [ ! -e "$RUNS/$name" ]; }
      note "<corpus>/runs/$name is absent now" "$(is absent_now)"
    done
    note "control: the quoted lines name no removal of P1's final run directory" "$(isnot removed_in_a1 "$KEEP")"
    nq=$(count_lines "$W/a1-removals")
    nstale=$(echo $STALE | wc -w)
    note "the quoted lines are exactly one command and one verdict per stale directory ($nq of 2 x $nstale)" "$(is [ "$nq" = "$((2 * nstale))" ])"
    # P2's own superseded run directories: no ruling covers them, so they are
    # kept, pending planning, and printed.
    for sup in "$DATE-$SHORT" "$DATE-$SHORT-b"; do
      if [ "$RUN" != "$sup" ] && [ -d "$RUNS/$sup" ]; then
        echo "  <corpus>/runs/$sup: a superseded P2 attempt's run directory; KEPT, pending planning (no ruling covers its removal)"
      fi
      sup_there() { [ -d "$RUNS/$sup" ]; }
      note "<corpus>/runs/$sup is still there, not removed by this log" "$(is sup_there)"
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## the entry check's own controls"
    # entries_p2 <entries> <id> <a> <chain> <parts file>: the runner's entry
    # rows for one workbook are what "Harness runs" expects. With A: the sheet
    # and workbook.xml changed, the content types and the workbook rels changed
    # when there is a chain and identical otherwise, the chain dropped; a
    # changed row may carry descriptor and nothing else; every other row
    # identical and unflagged. Without A every row identical and unflagged.
    # Names are read here and never printed.
    entries_p2() {
      local sheet wb rels cpart
      sheet=$(sed -n 1p "$5"); wb=$(sed -n 2p "$5"); rels=$(sed -n 3p "$5"); cpart=$(sed -n 4p "$5")
      awk -F'\t' -v id="$2" -v found="$3" -v chain="$4" -v sheet="$sheet" -v wb="$wb" \
          -v rels="$rels" -v cpart="$cpart" '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next }
        $k["id"] != id { next }
        {
          n++
          name = $k["name"]
          want = "identical"
          if (found == 1 && (name == sheet || name == wb)) want = "changed"
          if (found == 1 && chain == 1 && (name == rels || name == "[Content_Types].xml")) want = "changed"
          if (found == 1 && chain == 1 && name == cpart) want = "dropped"
          if ($k["status"] != want) bad++
          if (want == "changed" && $k["flags"] != "" && $k["flags"] != "descriptor") bad++
          if (want != "changed" && $k["flags"] != "") bad++
          if (want == "changed") nch++
          if (want == "dropped") ndr++
        }
        END {
          if (n == 0 || bad > 0) exit 1
          if (found == 1 && nch != (chain == 1 ? 4 : 2)) exit 1
          if (found == 1 && chain == 1 && ndr != 1) exit 1
        }' "$1"
    }
    printf 's.xml\nwb.xml\nr.rels\nc.xml\n' >"$W/parts-ctl"
    {
      printf 'id\tname\tstatus\tflags\n'
      printf 'w\ts.xml\tchanged\t\nw\twb.xml\tchanged\t\nw\tr.rels\tchanged\tdescriptor\n'
      printf 'w\t[Content_Types].xml\tchanged\t\nw\tc.xml\tdropped\t\nw\to.xml\tidentical\t\n'
    } >"$W/e-ctl.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 accepts the expected rows of a chained workbook" \
      "$(is entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" w 1 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    sed 's/o.xml\tidentical\t$/o.xml\tchanged\t/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-extra.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a fifth changed row" "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-extra.tsv" w 1 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    sed 's/c.xml\tdropped\t$/c.xml\tidentical\t/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-kept.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a chain left in place" "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-kept.tsv" w 1 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    sed 's/wb.xml\tchanged\t$/wb.xml\tchanged\trecompressed/' "$W/e-ctl.tsv" >"$W/e-flag.tsv"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses a changed row flagged anything but descriptor" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-flag.tsv" w 1 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses the chained rows for a workbook with no chain" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" w 1 0 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses changed rows for a workbook with no A" \
      "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" w 0 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    note "control: entries_p2 refuses an id with no rows" "$(isnot entries_p2 "$W/e-ctl.tsv" nosuchid 1 1 "$W/parts-ctl")"
    
    echo
    echo "## settings"
    echo "  --timeout 300 (the copy child only); --lo-timeout 600 (per conversion);"
    echo "  image $LO_IMAGE; --tool-arg $EDIT"
    echo "  out directory: <corpus>/runs/$RUN"
    echo "  record stem: $STEM; record directory: <scratch>/p2/out"
    manifest_rows=$(nrows "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv")
    echo "  corpus manifest rows: $manifest_rows (every later count of workbooks is compared with this, never with a typed number)"
    note "the corpus holds the 27 workbooks of the spec's Facts" "$(is [ "$manifest_rows" = 27 ])"
    { cat "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv"; printf 'planted\n'; } >"$W/manifest-plus"
    note "control: the same reader counts one more row on a manifest with one planted" \
      "$(is [ "$(nrows "$W/manifest-plus")" = "$((manifest_rows + 1))" ])"
    no_summary() {
      local f
      for f in "$1"/summary.*.tsv; do
        [ -e "$f" ] && return 1
      done
      return 0
    }
    mkdir -p "$W/ctl-run"
    note "control: no_summary accepts an empty directory" "$(is no_summary "$W/ctl-run")"
    : >"$W/ctl-run/summary.host.tsv"
    note "control: no_summary refuses a directory holding a summary" "$(isnot no_summary "$W/ctl-run")"
    note "the run directory <corpus>/runs/$RUN holds no summary before the runner" "$(is no_summary "$OUT")"
    if [ -e "$OUT/summary.host.tsv" ] || [ -e "$OUT/summary.i686.tsv" ]; then
      echo "  refusing to run over an earlier run's summary"
      exit 1
    fi
    
    # The log's own read of every input, once: pick and parts, never printed
    # beyond the counts.
    echo
    echo "## the log's own read of every input (counts only)"
    awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } { print $k["id"] "\t" $k["ext"] }' \
      "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" >"$W/ids"
    n_a=0; n_af=0; n_chain=0; n_chain_a=0; n_one_calc=0; n_flag=0
    while IFS=$'\t' read -r id ext; do
      in_file=$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext
      p=$(python3 "$PC" pick "$in_file")
      python3 "$PC" parts "$in_file" >"$W/parts-$id"
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$p" >>"$W/picks"
      echo "    $id $p"
      n_a=$((n_a + $(kvn "$p" a)))
      n_af=$((n_af + $(kvn "$p" a) * $(kvn "$p" f)))
      n_chain=$((n_chain + $(kvn "$p" chain)))
      n_chain_a=$((n_chain_a + $(kvn "$p" chain) * $(kvn "$p" a)))
      [ "$(kv "$p" calc_prs)" = 1 ] && n_one_calc=$((n_one_calc + 1))
      n_flag=$((n_flag + $(kvn "$p" calc_pr_flag)))
    done <"$W/ids"
    echo "  workbooks with A: $n_a; with A and F: $n_af; with a chain: $n_chain; with a chain and A: $n_chain_a; with one calcPr: $n_one_calc; with the flag already: $n_flag"
    echo "  so the expected totals: added $((2 * n_a)); replaced $n_af; chain_before $n_chain; chain_after $((n_chain - n_chain_a)); full_calc_after $n_a"
    echo "  the source of every expectation derived here: specs/0013 \"Planning rulings during P2 (2026-09-23)\", ruling 1"
    note "the log's own read finds the 9 chains of the spec's Facts" "$(is [ "$n_chain" = 9 ])"
    note "every workbook has exactly one calcPr (the spec's Facts)" "$(is [ "$n_one_calc" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
    note "no workbook carries fullCalcOnLoad (the spec's Facts)" "$(is [ "$n_flag" = 0 ])"
    pick_of() { awk -F'\t' -v id="$1" '$1 == id { print $2; exit }' "$W/picks"; }
    awk -F'\t' 'index($2, " a=0 ") { print $1 }' "$W/picks" | sort >"$W/no-a-ids"
    awk -F'\t' 'index($2, " a=1 ") { print $1 }' "$W/picks" | sort >"$W/a-ids"
    echo "  ids without A: $(count_lines "$W/no-a-ids"); ids with A: $(count_lines "$W/a-ids")"
    note "the ids with and without A cover the manifest's rows" \
      "$(is [ "$(( $(count_lines "$W/no-a-ids") + $(count_lines "$W/a-ids") ))" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
    
    for label in host i686; do
      if [ "$label" = host ]; then PT=$PT_host; XD=$XD_host; else PT=$PT_i686; XD=$XD_i686; fi
      echo
      echo "## $label run, --tool-arg $EDIT"
      echo "command: scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label $label --passthrough <scratch>/${PT#"$SCR"/} --xlsx-diff <scratch>/${XD#"$SCR"/} --out <corpus>/runs/$RUN --libreoffice $LO_IMAGE --lo-timeout 600 --timeout 300 --tool-arg $EDIT"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label "$label" --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" \
        --out "$OUT" --libreoffice "$LO_IMAGE" --lo-timeout 600 --timeout 300 \
        --tool-arg "$EDIT" \
        >"$W/run-$label.stdout" 2>"$W/run-$label.stderr"
      rc=$?
      ended=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      echo "  started $started; ended $ended; exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$W/run-$label.stderr")"
      hide <"$W/run-$label.stdout" | sed 's/^/    /'
      if [ -s "$W/run-$label.stderr" ]; then hide <"$W/run-$label.stderr" | sed 's/^/    stderr: /'; fi
      note "$label the run exits 0" "$(is [ "$rc" -eq 0 ])"
      note "$label the run's stderr is empty" "$(is [ "$(wc -c <"$W/run-$label.stderr")" -eq 0 ])"
      SUM=$OUT/summary.$label.tsv
      ENT=$OUT/entries.$label.tsv
      if [ ! -f "$SUM" ] || [ ! -f "$ENT" ]; then
        echo "  the run wrote no summary or entries file"; bad; continue
      fi
      rows=$(nrows "$SUM")
      ok=$(count_where "$SUM" outcome ok)
      lo=$(count_where "$SUM" lo ok)
      lo_in=$(count_where "$SUM" lo_in ok)
      noleft=$(count_where "$SUM" leftover no)
      order=$(count_where "$SUM" order_preserved yes)
      comment=$(count_where "$SUM" comment_equal yes)
      fid_yes=$(count_where "$SUM" files_identical yes)
      echo "  summary rows: $rows; outcome ok: $ok; lo ok: $lo; lo_in ok: $lo_in; leftover no: $noleft"
      echo "  order_preserved yes: $order; comment_equal yes: $comment; files_identical yes: $fid_yes"
      echo "  entry totals from the summary: identical $(sum_col "$SUM" identical), recompressed $(sum_col "$SUM" recompressed), changed $(sum_col "$SUM" changed), dropped $(sum_col "$SUM" dropped), added $(sum_col "$SUM" added), flagged $(sum_col "$SUM" flagged)"
      note "$label every manifest workbook produced a summary row" "$(is [ "$rows" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
      note "$label every outcome is ok" "$(is [ "$ok" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label lo is ok on every file" "$(is [ "$lo" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label lo_in is ok on every file" "$(is [ "$lo_in" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label no tool left a temporary behind" "$(is [ "$noleft" = "$rows" ])"
      note "$label the archive comment is unchanged in every file" "$(is [ "$comment" = "$rows" ])"
      echo "  the entries header, as the runner wrote it:"
      echo "    $(head -1 "$ENT")"
      note "$label every column the entry check indexes is in that header" \
        "$(is columns_resolve "$ENT" 'id name status flags')"
    
      echo "  per workbook: id, the tool's line, then the comparison's and the computation's verdicts (counts and yes/no only)"
      : >"$W/lines-$label"
      nagree=0; nent=0; ncmp=0; ncomp=0; ncomp_due=0
      t_added=0; t_replaced=0; t_cb=0; t_ca=0; t_fcb=0; t_fca=0; n_added2=0; n_added_ok=0
      while IFS=$'\t' read -r id ext; do
        in_file=$CORPUS/corpus/$id.$ext
        out_file=$OUT/$id/out.$label.$ext
        e=$(cat "$OUT/$id/stdout.$label.txt" 2>/dev/null)
        p=$(pick_of "$id")
        printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$e" >>"$W/lines-$label"
        printf '    %s %s\n' "$id" "$(printf '%s' "$e" | tr '\t' ' ')"
        if line_agrees "$e" "$p"; then nagree=$((nagree + 1)); else echo "    $id: THE TOOL'S LINE IS NOT THE ONE THE LOG'S OWN READ EXPECTS"; fi
        if entries_p2 "$ENT" "$id" "$(kv "$p" a)" "$(kv "$p" chain)" "$W/parts-$id"; then
          nent=$((nent + 1))
        else
          echo "    $id: an entry row is not what Harness runs expects"
        fi
        c=$(python3 "$PC" cmp "$in_file" "$out_file")
        echo "    $id cmp: $c"
        if cmp_holds "$c"; then ncmp=$((ncmp + 1)); else echo "    $id: THE COMPARISON DOES NOT HOLD"; fi
        if [ "$(kv "$p" a)" = 1 ]; then
          ncomp_due=$((ncomp_due + 1))
          cm=$(python3 "$PC" computed "$in_file" "$out_file" "$W/lo-work" "$LO_IMAGE" 600)
          echo "    $id computed: $cm"
          if computed_holds "$cm" "$(kv "$p" f)"; then ncomp=$((ncomp + 1)); else echo "    $id: THE COMPUTATION DOES NOT HOLD"; fi
        fi
        t_added=$((t_added + $(kvn "$e" added)))
        t_replaced=$((t_replaced + $(kvn "$e" replaced)))
        t_cb=$((t_cb + $(kvn "$e" chain_before)))
        t_ca=$((t_ca + $(kvn "$e" chain_after)))
        t_fcb=$((t_fcb + $(kvn "$e" full_calc_before)))
        t_fca=$((t_fca + $(kvn "$e" full_calc_after)))
        [ "$(kv "$e" added)" = 2 ] && n_added2=$((n_added2 + 1))
        [ "$(kvn "$e" added)" = "$((2 * $(kvn "$p" a)))" ] && n_added_ok=$((n_added_ok + 1))
      done <"$W/ids"
      converted_left() { [ -e "$W/lo-work" ]; }
      note "$label no converted file outlives its read" "$(isnot converted_left)"
      echo "  workbooks: $manifest_rows; the tool's line as the log's own read expects: $nagree; entry rows as expected: $nent; comparison holding: $ncmp; computation holding: $ncomp of $ncomp_due"
      echo "  $label totals from the tool's lines: added $t_added; replaced $t_replaced; chain_before $t_cb; chain_after $t_ca; full_calc_before $t_fcb; full_calc_after $t_fca; workbooks with added 2: $n_added2"
      note "$label every tool line is the one the log's own read expects" "$(is [ "$nagree" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
      note "$label every workbook's entry rows are as Harness runs expects" "$(is [ "$nent" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
      note "$label the comparison holds on every output" "$(is [ "$ncmp" = "$manifest_rows" ])"
      note "$label the computation holds on every output with A" "$(is [ "$ncomp" = "$ncomp_due" ])"
      # Ruling 1's expectations, each derived from the log's own read, each
      # with a control that offers the same comparison a value one off.
      n_ct=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next }
        $k["name"] == "[Content_Types].xml" && $k["status"] == "changed" { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$ENT")
      n_drop=$(count_where "$ENT" status dropped)
      n_chg=$(count_where "$ENT" status changed)
      echo "  $label entry classes: changed rows $n_chg; content types changed $n_ct; dropped $n_drop; files_identical yes $fid_yes"
      echo "  $label expectations (ruling 1, from the log's own read): added 2 on each of $n_a workbooks with A; replaced $n_af; chain_before $n_chain; chain_after $((n_chain - n_chain_a)); full_calc_before $n_flag; full_calc_after $n_a; changed rows $((2 * n_a + 2 * n_chain_a)); content types changed $n_chain_a; dropped $n_chain_a; files_identical yes $((manifest_rows - n_a))"
      derived_eq() { [ "$1" = "$2" ]; }
      check_derived() {
        note "$label $1 (ruling 1): $2 against $3" "$(is derived_eq "$2" "$3")"
        note "$label control: the same comparison refuses $1 one off ($(($3 + 1)))" "$(isnot derived_eq "$2" "$(($3 + 1))")"
      }
      check_derived "added is 2 on each workbook with A, 0 on the others (workbooks so, of the manifest's rows)" "$n_added_ok" "$manifest_rows"
      check_derived "added totals 2 per workbook with A" "$t_added" "$((2 * n_a))"
      check_derived "replaced equals the workbooks with A and F" "$t_replaced" "$n_af"
      check_derived "chain_before equals the chained workbooks" "$t_cb" "$n_chain"
      check_derived "chain_after equals chain_before minus the chained workbooks with A" "$t_ca" "$((n_chain - n_chain_a))"
      check_derived "full_calc_before equals the inputs already flagged" "$t_fcb" "$n_flag"
      check_derived "full_calc_after equals the workbooks with A" "$t_fca" "$n_a"
      check_derived "the workbooks with added 2 are the workbooks with A" "$n_added2" "$n_a"
      check_derived "changed rows are the sheet and workbook.xml per A, and the content types and rels per chained A" "$n_chg" "$((2 * n_a + 2 * n_chain_a))"
      check_derived "the content types change only on the chained workbooks with A" "$n_ct" "$n_chain_a"
      check_derived "the chain entry goes only on the chained workbooks with A" "$n_drop" "$n_chain_a"
      check_derived "the count of files_identical yes equals the workbooks without A" "$fid_yes" "$((manifest_rows - n_a))"
      # F8: the same as sets of ids, not only as counts.
      awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next }
        $k["files_identical"] == "yes" { print $k["id"] }' "$SUM" | sort >"$W/fid-ids-$label"
      note "$label the ids with files_identical yes are exactly the ids without A" \
        "$(is cmp -s "$W/fid-ids-$label" "$W/no-a-ids")"
      swap_one() { sed '1d' "$1"; head -n 1 "$W/a-ids"; }
      swap_one "$W/no-a-ids" | sort >"$W/no-a-swapped"
      note "$label control: the same comparison refuses the set with one id swapped for an id with A" \
        "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/fid-ids-$label" "$W/no-a-swapped")"
    
      # The plants on one REAL output: the first workbook with A, F and a chain.
      # Every comparison plant must apply and turn its flag alone, and one
      # computation plant must be caught.
      real=$(awk -F'\t' '{ if (index($2, " a=1 f=1 chain=1 ")) { print $1; exit } }' "$W/picks")
      if [ -n "$real" ]; then
        rext=$(awk -F'\t' -v id="$real" '$1 == id { print $2 }' "$W/ids")
        rin=$CORPUS/corpus/$real.$rext
        rout=$OUT/$real/out.$label.$rext
        nreal=0
        for flag in $CMP_FLAGS; do
          pl=$(python3 "$PC" cmp "$rin" "$rout" --plant "$flag")
          if only_flag_no "$pl" "$flag"; then nreal=$((nreal + 1)); else echo "    $real plant $flag: not caught alone"; fi
        done
        note "$label control: on $real's output all 15 comparison plants apply and turn their flag alone" \
          "$(is [ "$nreal" = 15 ])"
        rc_line=$(python3 "$PC" computed "$rin" "$rout" "$W/lo-work" "$LO_IMAGE" 600 --plant v_new1)
        echo "    $real computed plant v_new1: $rc_line"
        note "$label control: on $real's output the planted v_new1 is caught alone" \
          "$(is computed_plant_caught "$rc_line" v_new1 1)"
      else
        echo "  no workbook with A, F and a chain for the real-output controls"; bad
      fi
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## the two labels agree"
    for label in host i686; do
      awk -F'\t' '
        NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) idx[$i] = i; next }
        { print $idx["id"] "\t" $idx["name"] "\t" $idx["status"] "\t" $idx["flags"] }' \
        "$OUT/entries.$label.tsv" | sort >"$W/classes-$label"
      sort "$W/lines-$label" >"$W/lines-sorted-$label"
    done
    note "both targets classified every entry the same way" "$(is cmp -s "$W/classes-host" "$W/classes-i686")"
    note "both targets printed the same line for every workbook" \
      "$(is cmp -s "$W/lines-sorted-host" "$W/lines-sorted-i686")"
    same_outputs() {
      local id ext
      while IFS=$'\t' read -r id ext; do
        cmp -s "$OUT/$id/out.host.$ext" "$OUT/$id/out.i686.$ext" || return 1
      done <"$W/ids"
    }
    note "both targets wrote byte-identical outputs" "$(is same_outputs)"
    sed '1s/added=\([0-9]\)/added=X/' "$W/lines-sorted-i686" >"$W/lines-planted"
    note "control: the same comparison finds one planted line differ" \
      "$(isnot cmp -s "$W/lines-sorted-host" "$W/lines-planted")"
    
    echo
    echo "## the run rows both labels appended"
    for label in host i686; do
      R=$OUT/run.$label.tsv
      if [ -f "$R" ]; then
        echo "  run.$label.tsv header: $(head -1 "$R")"
        echo "  run.$label.tsv row: $(sed -n 2p "$R" | hide)"
        args=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "tool_args") k = i; next }
                           k && NR == 2 { print $k }' "$R")
        echo "  run.$label.tsv tool_args: [$args]"
        note "$label the run row records the operation" "$(is [ "$args" = "$EDIT" ])"
      else
        echo "  run.$label.tsv: MISSING"; bad
      fi
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## the record pair (written to <scratch>/p2/out)"
    echo "command: scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <corpus>/runs/$RUN --out <scratch>/p2/out --stem $STEM"
    scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$OUT" --out "$REC_DIR" --stem "$STEM" >"$W/record.out" 2>&1
    rrc=$?
    hide <"$W/record.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
    note "the record script exits 0" "$(is [ "$rrc" -eq 0 ])"
    for ext in md txt; do
      f=$REC_DIR/$STEM.$ext
      if [ -f "$f" ]; then
        echo "  <scratch>/p2/out/$STEM.$ext: $(wc -c <"$f") bytes, sha256 $(sha256sum <"$f" | cut -d' ' -f1)"
      else
        echo "  <scratch>/p2/out/$STEM.$ext: MISSING"; bad
      fi
    done
    both_halves() {
      [ -f "$REC_DIR/$STEM.md" ] || return 1
      [ -f "$REC_DIR/$STEM.txt" ] || return 1
    }
    note "both halves of the record pair were written" "$(is both_halves)"
    nargs=$(count_matches -F "$EDIT" "$REC_DIR/$STEM.md")
    echo "  lines of the record naming the operation: $nargs"
    note "the record names the operation it was run with" "$(is [ "$nargs" -ge 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the record pair holds no corpus path and no absolute path"
    for ext in md txt; do
      f=$REC_DIR/$STEM.$ext
      [ -f "$f" ] || continue
      n=$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$f")
      echo "  <scratch>/p2/out/$STEM.$ext: lines naming a home, mount, temporary or corpus path: $n"
      note "$STEM.$ext carries no such path" "$(is [ "$n" = 0 ])"
    done
    printf '%s%s%s\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x.xlsx' >"$W/path-control"
    nctl=$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$W/path-control")
    note "control: the path form finds a planted path ($nctl)" "$(is [ "$nctl" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the runs"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_phase=$(run_matches -E "$PHASE_FILES" git status --porcelain)
    planning_status
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs or record pair: $st_phase; planning's files modified: $st_plan"
    note "every change in the working tree is this phase's logs or record pair, or planning's file" \
      "$(is status_accounted "$st_all" "$st_phase" "$st_plan")"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "verdict rows other than as-expected: $nbad; of them marked UNEXPECTED: $nunexp"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources
command: sed 's/^/    /' scripts/counting.sh; sha256 60a379312a5681cba0c1acfb128402c95fa1ec753158d1b29962bce2320e742c
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "$d"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

## counting controls
  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on a file with none: 0 (expect 0)
  control count_matches summed over two files: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches with a regular expression: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: error (expect error)
  control count_from_file on the same file: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_from_file on a file with none: 0 (expect 0)
  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: 3 (expect 3)
  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_bytes on a clean file: 0 (expect 0)
  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control count_lines on a three-line file: 3 (expect 3)
  control count_lines on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control count_matches_i on mixed case: 2 (expect 2)
  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: 1 (expect 1)
  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: error (expect error)
  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: 3 (expect 3)
  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: 0 (expect 0)
  control run_lines on a FAILING command: error (expect error)
  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: error (expect error)
